<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 18_responsive/03: Fluid type with clamp -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Fluid type with clamp</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .fluid h2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1rem + 3vw, 3.5rem); margin: 0; line-height: 1.1; }
    .fluid p { font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.9rem + 0.4vw, 1.25rem); max-width: 60ch; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Fluid type with clamp</h1>
    <p class="lead">Headings that scale smoothly between a minimum and a maximum.</p>
    <div class="fluid"><h2>Fluid headline</h2><p>Resize the window: the text grows with the viewport but never below or above its limits.</p></div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
